# Scholarly domain rules

- Read `docs/01-domain/DOMAIN_MAP.md`, `GLOSSARY.md`, `EDITORIAL_LIFECYCLE.md`, and `CONTENT_AND_JATS.md` before touching domain logic.
- Use explicit state transitions and domain/application use cases; never mutate workflow status arbitrarily.
- Keep Article, ArticleVersion, Publication, Issue, Journal, and external identifiers distinct.
- Preserve provenance, version history, actor, timestamp, and reason for editorial/production/publishing changes.
- Model structured article content and JATS interoperability; do not make PDF the canonical content source.
- Crossref, ORCID, ROR, OAI-PMH, indexing, and preservation are external integrations; isolate them behind adapters and record verification status.
- Human editors retain academic decision authority.
